            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "core.c",
                    "line": 542,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Richard Marian Thomaiyar",
                        "email": "richard.marian.thomaiyar@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "rthomaiy"
                    },
                    "message": "1. We are going to have a problem here, when bridging concept (in review) by andrew get's merged. \nIn case of bridging, there will be a chance that it is the only packet, and we can't even find EOM packet for it (as it will come late). So, we need to watch other stuff as well. (i.e. EID / MsgTag along with EOM monitoring, or else it's better to have a index count / relation count in the pkt so that the same can be dropped)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "core.c",
                    "line": 542,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "That's a fair point; the optimisation was based on the assumption that we were queuing entire messages-worth of packets. Seems James had it right :)"
                },
