                    "message": "hmm i meant to say re-using existing erorr codes \nSay EBUSY or  something to tell that interface is busy and retry it at later stage, rest of the error, we don't need to stop, we continue with next packet processing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "core.c",
                    "line": 551,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not opposed to a proper errno. We might want to eventually do some analysis and define our own errnos so we don't leak unix-y implementation details through the API (but leaning on unix-y solutions is a cheap and cheerful place to start)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "core.c",
