                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Richard Marian Thomaiyar",
                        "email": "richard.marian.thomaiyar@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "rthomaiy"
                    },
                    "message": "we should break only if it is due to tx_enabled == false error, for other packets we must continue\ni.e. Just because one packet transmission failed, we shouldn't break for others, we must continue till the queue is empty or till tx_enabled becomes false."
                },
                {
                    "file": "core.c",
                    "line": 571,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think that's a strong requirement. Packets will always end up in the queue and the queue will eventually be processed. I think what you're concerned about is latency. That's probably a wider discussion."
                },
                {
