                        "username": "rthomaiy"
                    },
                    "message": "this is going to cause confusion.\ni.e. \nWith current code in place, we may end up sending error of the packet which is already in queue, which is getting dropped and it will cause confusion.\n\nElse we need to ignore tx_enabled == false error, and can propagate only the last transmission error to the packet (when we transmit the whole queue). \n\nAnyway, application can never know this one for sure, and hence there is no point in indicating error through this mechanism."
